<title>CHILE: Chile's Madeco buys Brazil cable maker.</title>
<headline>Chile's Madeco buys Brazil cable maker.</headline>
<dateline>SANTIAGO 1997-01-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Chilean copper products maker Madeco SA said it has bought a 67 percent stake in Brazil's second largest cable manufacturer, FICAP SA, for $121.1 million.</p>
<p>This is the first investment by Madeco, which already has projects in Argentina, Peru and Uruguay, in the giant Brazilian market.</p>
<p>&quot;The acquisition of the majority shares in FICAP will allow Madeco to extend its activities in this area to a market with high growth and development potential,&quot; said the statement.</p>
</text>
